@style(../styles/IDocDemo.style)
@title(Charts: Maps)

Choropleths, slippy maps, globes and street imagery, all offline. Each chart is followed by the source that drew it, and every example carries its own data.

@table(widths=equal)
@row
@cell
@b{Choropleth}

Regions shaded by value.

@graph(type=choropleth, geo=us-states, region=State, value=Rate, title="By state")
@data
State,Rate
California,7.2
Texas,6.1
New York,5.4
@end

@code(idoc)
@graph(type=choropleth, geo=us-states, region=State, value=Rate, title="By state")
@data
State,Rate
California,7.2
Texas,6.1
New York,5.4
@end
@end
@endcell
@cell
@b{Slippy map}

A zoomable, pannable basemap drawn on the GPU from local blocks — no tiles, no API calls.

@graph(type=map, basemap=dark, center=-74.0,40.7, zoom=10)

@code(idoc)
@graph(type=map, basemap=dark, center=-74.0,40.7, zoom=10)
@end

Styles: dark, light, blueprint. Plot data over it with lon=/lat=, or layer=heatmap.
@endcell
@endtable

@table(widths=equal)
@row
@cell
@b{Globe}

A rotatable 3-D globe, in any projection.

@graph(type=globe, projection=Orthographic)

@code(idoc)
@graph(type=globe, projection=Orthographic)
@end

Projections: Natural, Mercator, EqualEarth, Orthographic, AzimuthalEqualArea, Equirectangular.
@endcell
@cell
@b{Street imagery}

Street-level photography with a coverage mini-map, packed offline.

@graph(type=street)

@code(idoc)
@graph(type=street)
@end

With no src= it shows a Midtown-NYC demo; point src= at a .bstr pack for your own area.
@endcell
@endtable
